WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.356
- Cycling as a sport, as a
hobby, and as a recreation,

00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:05.170
is just something that's
opened up to everybody,

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.160
and I think that's one of
the nice things about Dubai

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.671
is that you find yourself
becoming a big family.

00:00:09.671 --> 00:00:11.804
And Dubai welcomes everything like that.

00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:14.611
(bright music)

00:00:14.611 --> 00:00:15.680
(wheel spinning)

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.380
The wind blowing, and it's
raising your heart rate up.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.090
Everything else just starts to calm down.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.320
You're just out there,
completely you on your own,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.632
there's a wash of calm
that just comes over you.

00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:31.215
(bright music)

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.000
- My name is Mark Beaumont,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.447
and I'm an endurance athlete
with the current world record

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:40.263
for cycling around the planet.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.170
Seeking adventures and finding stories

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.780
is what I'm most passionate about.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:46.613
(motorcycle revs)

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.850
Ever since I can remember,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.275
I've had that sense of
curiosity about the world.

00:00:50.275 --> 00:00:52.780
(splash)

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.543
This time I've come to Dubai.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.474
Today I'm meeting Stewart
to find out how Dubai's

00:01:01.474 --> 00:01:03.623
cycling community is growing.

00:01:04.504 --> 00:01:06.460
- When you get out in the
morning on the Al Qudra

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.403
cycle track and the sun
rises over the desert,

00:01:08.403 --> 00:01:10.829
there's just that palette
of oranges and blues

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:12.138
reflecting through,

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.250
and it's so quiet and so serene out there

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.995
that I don't think that
there's many places on Earth

00:01:16.995 --> 00:01:19.229
that are as beautiful or as picturesque

00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:20.190
to go out and ride.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:24.210
As it is now to what it
was eight nine years ago,

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.310
an immense change.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.616
Now we have probably
what is the most iconic

00:01:28.616 --> 00:01:30.980
cycling route in the world.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.066
- What a dream as a bike rider,

00:01:33.066 --> 00:01:34.930
saying can we build you a
cycle track in the desert?

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.960
- Seven eight years ago,
there was a handful of us

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:39.210
out here on Al Qudra.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.140
Now on a Friday or Saturday morning,

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.900
I'd say there are thousands
of people out here.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.060
- So what's the plan from here?

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.750
- So now we're gonna
go and find some hills

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.366
out in Hatta, the Hajj mountain.

00:01:47.366 --> 00:01:49.571
You can see what the
hills in Dubai look like.

00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:51.462
- Superb, let's do it.

00:01:51.462 --> 00:01:54.212
(mystical music)

00:02:18.523 --> 00:02:20.050
Do you see more and more riders out here,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:20.937
or do they tend to
stick close to the city?

00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:23.560
- So good because it is a
nice different challenge

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.440
to people to come out to the mountains.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.770
You think you're gonna be the
only one when you get here,

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.440
and yeah, good couple hundred
riders out in a group.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.800
- I'm used to the highlands of Scotland,

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.440
but these are certainly drier rockier

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.274
At this time of day, you can
kinda see the way the light

00:02:36.274 --> 00:02:39.870
is starting to change and sort
of cast those deep shadows.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.520
- I think you're gonna have
to take a big deep breath now.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.860
Alley oop!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:44.693
- Deep breath

00:02:49.516 --> 00:02:51.849
(breathing)

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.209
It's another world up from the desert.

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:57.792
(upbeat music)

00:03:05.407 --> 00:03:09.330
Do you also kinda find
that cycling gives people

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.980
a different perspective on
Dubai because a lot of people,

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.090
if they've not been here, or
maybe they've been on holiday,

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.570
will just picture that.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.780
- There's so many things
that happen outside

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.241
of the vibrant city that is Dubai.

00:03:19.241 --> 00:03:23.000
You're a stone's throw
away from a hustling bustle

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.580
of a vibrant city.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.960
You're a stone's throw
away out into the desert

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.939
to go and cycle or up to
Hatta Mountains to go play

00:03:29.939 --> 00:03:31.013
in the mountains.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.260
The lakes out on Al Qudra,

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:35.990
the cycle track, the desert safaris,

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.120
the camping that goes out,

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.230
it's just an amazing place to live.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.803
- Superb, let's crack on.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.250
Year on year, Dubai changes insanely fast,

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.245
the infrastructure, the build,

00:03:52.245 --> 00:03:53.726
certainly when it comes to cycling,

00:03:53.726 --> 00:03:55.606
I mean I've seen it in my
world as a professional

00:03:55.606 --> 00:03:56.600
bike rider.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.170
In the last ten years,
that's just exploded

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.700
in popularity globally.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.520
And here in Dubai, it's
been matched with building

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:06.555
of cycle tracks and huge
investment and events

00:04:06.555 --> 00:04:08.530
popping up all over the place.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:10.528
I can see through spending
quality time with Stewart,

00:04:10.528 --> 00:04:11.856
he's just passionate about the sport.

00:04:11.856 --> 00:04:13.333
He loves sharing that.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:18.856
To land here and see
somebody who is so ingrained

00:04:18.856 --> 00:04:20.795
in the culture and
trying to make a change,

00:04:20.795 --> 00:04:22.983
to this great place to ride.

00:04:32.177 --> 00:04:34.094
(tone)

